# DPPS Build Rules (always apply)

## Source of truth
- docs/DPPS_Phase1_Design_v2.md is the final design. Follow it exactly.
- Do not add, remove or change tables, fields, rules, screens, roles or settings that are not in it.
- Never build anything from Section 15 (Phase 2 Parking Lot).
- If the design is unclear or contradictory: STOP and ask. Never guess.

## Step discipline
- Work only on the current step of the BUILD PLAN (see docs/PROGRESS.md).
- Never start or partly prepare the next step.
- Before reporting, run what you can (migrations, tests, build, lint) and fix any errors.
- End every step with the STEP REPORT and STOP. Wait for the user to reply "CONFIRMED".
- When the user reports a problem, fix only that problem inside the current step, then STOP again.
- Update docs/PROGRESS.md at the end of every step.

## Stay focused
- Only touch files needed for the current step.
- To change a file from a confirmed step, ask first and explain what and why.
- No refactoring, renaming or reformatting of working code unless asked.
- No new packages beyond those named in the design or master prompt without asking.
- No invented features or "nice to have" extras. Suggestions go in the report only.
- Never edit a migration from a confirmed step. Create a new migration instead.
- Never delete files, tables or data without asking.
- Every TODO or placeholder must be listed in the step report.

## Architecture
- Laravel 12 REST API under /api/v1 in /backend; Vue 3 + Vite + Pinia + PrimeVue SPA in /frontend.
- All business rules live in the backend (form requests, services, policies). The mobile app will reuse the API.
- Every API query enforces data scope: own company for company users, own district for District Officers.
- Warnings use HTTP 409 with a `warnings` array. The client resends with `confirm_warnings: true` and `warning_reason`, which is logged.
- Every create, update, delete, login, download, export, approval and override is written to activity_logs.
- Fees have no screen and no write API.
